Minutes of Meeting — MXRAP Capstone Project

Date: 22/09/2026
Duration: 33 minutes
Attendees: Viktor Kim, Warson Long, Shantanu Sharma, Amritansh Kaur Mamotra, Lola Xu and Hongfei Peng.

Purpose: Review development progress, identify outstanding work, clarify responsibilities and discuss upcoming assessments.

1. Development progress

The team reviewed the current application, including point markers, point inspection, annotations and surface rendering.

Surface rendering was largely implemented but required testing before the task could be closed.
Additional test cases were needed.

2. Charts, dashboards and time series

Viktor raised concerns about the client’s expectations for charts, dashboards and comparisons between time snapshots. He noted that these features were included in the technical specification at a lower priority.

The team discussed adding a separate charts section. No implementation approach was finalised. Client clarification and additional sample data were needed before proceeding.

3. Marker colours and date filtering

The team identified a discrepancy between the multicolour legend and points appearing white in one test dataset. A larger export displayed different colours after refreshing the application.

The following work was identified:

Investigate and correct marker colour mapping.
Confirm the appropriate legend range and interpretation of ML values.
Implement filtering by date and time.

Shantanu offered to work on date/time filtering and marker colours.

4. Client clarification and software access

The team discussed requesting the following from Matt:

Clarification of expected charts, dashboards and scenes.
Additional sample data.
Screenshots or a walkthrough showing the original MXRAP views alongside matching exported data.
A temporary MXRAP licence to help compare the application with the source software.

Viktor offered to contact Matt about requirements and reference material. Amritansh later volunteered to request the temporary licence.

5. Task allocation and contribution tracking

Shantanu raised concerns about overlapping assignments and work being completed by other members before the assigned person could contribute.
The team discussed reviewing completed features and identifying remaining improvements and testing tasks.
Members agreed to create tickets assigned to themselves and reference the relevant issue numbers in commit messages.

